module code;

// A value committed into per-connection state that outlives the callback
// writing it. Transport libraries hand the same store to the authentication
// callbacks and to the established session, so whatever a pre-verification
// callback writes is still there when the session starts.
//
// Declares no vulnerableTo on purpose. The sink labels every value written
// through the store's setter; the finding comes from the pairing with
// code.UnverifiedCredential, and a correct program has no path between them
// because the identity is derived after authentication. The clearing control
// is the dataflow, so there is no check concept to bind per language.
concept ConnectionStateWrite : sink {
  cwe: [CWE_287]
  enabledBy: [taint.UntrustedData]
}
